cli_result.result:
{"content":"Fixed the regression: `Identifier.get_array_indices()` in sqlparse/sql.py had an inverted condition (`if not (isinstance(token, SquareBrackets))`) that caused it to skip actual SquareBrackets tokens and instead yield contents of unrelated tokens. Changed it to `if isinstance(token, SquareBrackets)`. Verified with manual tests covering simple 1d array index, 2d array index, and schema-qualified array index — all now correctly return the index token lists (e.g., `a[1]` -> `['1']`, `a[1][2]` -> `['1','2']`, `schema.a[1]` -> `['1']`). This should also fix the 4th related failing case (likely a function-call array index or similar variant using the same method).","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_1","name":"run","arguments":{"command":"python -c "import sqlparse
p = sqlparse.parse('SELECT func()[1]')[0]
for t in p.tokens:
    print(repr(t))
